 ## Overview
-Morphological dilation expands the set of foreground voxels in a voxel grid by propagating the "filled" state to neighboring voxels based on a defined connectivity kernel [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of surface thinning, gaps, or insufficient thickness in solid voxelizations by ensuring that any voxel adjacent to a filled voxel is also considered filled [S2, unofficial]. It is distinguished from its sibling [VoxelGrid from Mesh (Fill Method)](1013-voxelgrid-from-mesh-fill-method.md) by being a post-processing step applied to an already generated solid voxel grid, rather than a primary filling algorithm during voxelization [S2, unofficial].
+Morphological dilation expands the set of foreground voxels in a voxel grid by propagating the filled state to neighboring voxels based on a defined connectivity kernel [S1, unofficial]. It creates a hierarchical structure that allows rapid queries on whether a neighborhood contains filled voxels, which is useful for applications like pathfinding or visibility [S2, unofficial]. It is distinguished from its sibling [VoxelGrid from Mesh (Fill Method)](1013-voxelgrid-from-mesh-fill-method.md) by being a purely image-based post-processing step applied to an already generated solid voxel grid [S2, unofficial].
