 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Boundary Conditions:** The algorithm typically iterates only over internal voxels ($1$ to $dim-2$). Boundary voxels remain unchanged, which may leave the outer shell of the voxel grid un-dilated [S1, unofficial]. To dilate boundaries, padding or explicit boundary handling is required.
-- **Connectivity Choice:** 26-connectivity produces a more spherical expansion but is computationally more expensive (26 checks vs 6). 6-connectivity is faster but results in a "cross-shaped" expansion [S1, unofficial].
-- **Precision:** Since the operation is binary (logical OR), floating-point precision is not a concern. However, integer overflow is not an issue as values are clamped to 0/1.
