 - **Performance:** On GPU hardware (e.g., NVidia 6800, 8800 GTS), this operation is fast because it is purely image-based and avoids complex geometric preprocessing [S2, unofficial]. It can be implemented in a single pass using fragment shaders with MRT (Multiple Render Targets) support [S2, unofficial].
-- **Strengths:** Simple to implement, fast on GPU, effective for closing small gaps and thickening surfaces in voxel data [S2, unofficial].
-- **Limitations:** Does not handle boundary voxels by default; connectivity choice affects shape fidelity; iterative dilation for large radii increases computational cost [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
