 - **When to use:** When a solid voxelization already exists and needs to be thickened or gaps closed for applications like pathfinding or visibility queries [S2, unofficial].
 - **When not to use:** When precise surface representation is critical without expansion, or when boundary voxels must be included without padding.
 
 ## Background
-Morphological operations on voxel grids originate from mathematical morphology in image processing, adapted for 3D voxel data [S2, unofficial]. The specific application to solid voxelization for real-time rendering and applications like pathfinding was detailed in research on single-pass GPU solid voxelization [S2, unofficial]. The method leverages the binary nature of voxel grids to use efficient logical operations and bit-shifting techniques [S2, unofficial].
